  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 513.08 Antique Trailer Plate.\n\n(a) Antique trailer plates shall be issued, upon request, to vehicles meeting the definition of RSA 261:89-a, I, provided that the trailer is over 25 years old as specified in (b) below.\n\n(b) An applicant for antique trailer plates shall provide proof of trailer age by presenting:\n\n(1) A title which reflects more than a 25 year old date of manufacture;\n\n(2) A registration which reflects more than a 25 year old date of manufacture; or\n\n(3) A statement, signed under penalty of unsworn falsification pursuant to RSA 641:3, from the current owner containing the facts which demonstrate that the trailer is more than 25 years old.\n\n(c) Antique trailer plates shall:\n\n(1) Have the words “ANTIQUE TRAILER” on the right vertical border; and\n\n(2) Have 3 to 5 characters, 2 of which shall be the letters “AT”, and the remainder of which shall be numerals.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 514.08)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
